CHANGES
LATCH (2)
  alu.v: Initialize the 33-bit tmp to 33'd0 at entry to the combinational
  block. The arithmetic branches still overwrite tmp before reading it.
  instr_decode.v: Initialize opc to 7'd0 before testing reset. Normal
  instruction decode still takes opc from instr[6:0].

SYNCASYNCNET (1)
  pc.v and riscv_core.v: Remove posedge reset from the PC and MMIO state
  processes. All CPU state now samples active-high reset at posedge clk,
  matching the register file and data memory. Reset must be present at a
  rising edge. PC and MMIO no longer clear immediately between edges.
  The combinational reset gating in decode and control remains in place.
  Synthesis/init_design/test_init_elab.py now expects the PC process to
  have only a rising-clock event.

UNUSEDSIGNAL (2)
  data_mem.v and inst_mem.v: Use addr[31:10] and addr[1:0] to check the
  memory region and word alignment. Each 256 x 32 memory accepts aligned
  byte addresses 0x00000000 through 0x000003fc. The word index remains
  addr[9:2]. High or misaligned addresses previously aliased valid words.
  Invalid data writes are ignored, invalid data reads return zero, and
  invalid instruction fetches return the existing RISC-V NOP encoding.
  These are baseline memory-map choices for this core. No trap or
  exception is generated. The separate MMIO write at 0x00007000 remains.

